<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palazzo Te</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1524–1534</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Palazzo Te is a villa on the edge of Mantua, built between 1524 and 1534 for Federico II Gonzaga to designs by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giulio-romano">Giulio Romano</a>. Conceived as a pleasure palace, it is a landmark of Mannerist architecture. Its frescoed rooms include the Room of the Giants, where the walls seem to collapse on the viewer.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palazzo-te.jpg" alt="Palazzo Te" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FrDr · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mantova_104.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
